+name: Stepper happy path (canonical F1 drive)
+description: |
+  The canonical F1 scenario — the same employed solo applicant as
+  happy-path/employed-with-rental-history, but driven THROUGH the stepper
+  (no stepper=off). Exercises the full wiring the node tests can't:
+  chrome renders ("Step 1 of 8 — About You"), sections 2–8 hidden at init,
+  Continue gates on an empty visible required field (assert the block on
+  step 1: status stays, inline "This one's needed before you continue."
+  appears, focus moves to first_name), gated advance per section, Back
+  preserves entered values, file gating on documents, consent-gated
+  submit on review, confirmation.
+  Driving: fill only the CURRENT section's fields, click its
+  [data-testid=step-continue-<section_id>] (section ids in DOM order:
+  about_you, your_situation, work_income, references, guarantor,
+  tell_us_more, documents, review_consent). The address quartet is inside
+  the collapsed <details data-testid="address-cluster"> — open it on the
+  your_situation step before filling. ATTESTATION GATING (F1×RC1.2): on
+  the references step, click Continue BEFORE answering the attestation
+  card and assert the block — status stays on "Step 4 of 8 — References"
+  and the card shows the §5.3 "Choose one option to continue." message —
+  then click [data-testid=ref-attestation-yes] and Continue through.
