+# Blind Hunter — adversarial review, form-stepper-f1
+
+Reviewed cold against the diff, the spec of record, and the on-disk source
+(`form_stepper.js`, `form.js`, `apply_analytics.js`, `form_sections/*`,
+`form_fields.gleam`, `error_summary.gleam`, `form_pages.gleam`, `.gitignore`,
+tests). `make test-server` (1131 pass), `node --test scripts/js-tests/*` (46
+pass), and `gleam format --check` are all green — every finding below
+survives a green build.
+
+1. **Blocker — `.gitignore:31` — `form_stepper.js` is git-ignored; the feature never ships.**
+   `.gitignore` has `server/priv/static/*` with a per-file whitelist
+   (`form.css`, `form.js`, `apply_analytics.js`, `consent.js`, …) that was
+   not extended for the new file. `git status` shows no trace of
+   `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js`; `git add -A` will not pick it up.
+   Either CI fails (the committed `scripts/js-tests/form_stepper.test.js`
+   `require()`s the missing module), or — worse — the script tags ship
+   without the file: `/static/form_stepper.js` 404s in production, the
+   stepper silently never runs, and every SSR pin still passes because they
+   only assert the `<script>` tag exists. The whole F1 feature would deploy
+   as a dead tag.
+   **Fix:** add `!server/priv/static/form_stepper.js` to `.gitignore` next to
+   the `apply_analytics.js` line and `git add -f` the file.
+
+2. **High — `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js:438-443` — error-summary anchor routing is dead for every link.**
+   The banner renders `href="#field-<key>"` (`form_pages.gleam` `view_error_row`
+   → `error_summary.anchor_for` = `"field-" <> key`). The click handler does
+   `id = href.slice(1)` → `"field-email"` and passes it to
+   `resolveFieldElement`, which prepends again → `getElementById("field-field-email")`
+   → null; the testid fallback likewise looks for `field-field-email` → null →
+   `return` **without** `preventDefault`. The browser's native anchor jump then
+   targets an element inside a `hidden` section: no scroll, no focus, no step
+   switch. The spec's error re-render acceptance row ("summary links switch
+   steps + focus the field") fails for 100% of links pointing outside the
+   current step — the exact scenario the stepper-on-error-page exists for.
+   Unit tests escape it because they only call `resolveFieldElement` with raw
+   keys, never through the click path.
+   **Fix:** strip the prefix before resolving
+   (`resolveFieldElement(doc, id.replace(/^field-/, ""))`) or try
+   `doc.getElementById(id)` first, and add a click-level test using a real
+   `#field-<key>` href.
+
+3. **Medium — `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js:353` (`onContinue`) — a preflight-blocked file passes gating and dead-ends the submit on step 8.**
+   Gating checks only `files.length` (`controlSatisfied`), so an applicant who
+   stages a 6MB file on the documents step sails through Continue while
+   form.js's preflight has already set `data-preflight-blocked` on the submit
+   button. On step 8 the consent checkbox re-runs `__rtRecomputeSubmitDisabled`,
+   which keeps the button disabled — with zero visible explanation, because the
+   reason (an inline `.field-error` on the documents step) is now hidden, and
+   is itself `display:none` (see finding 8). Pre-stepper the applicant could at
+   least scroll back to the documents area; the stepper removes even that cue.
+   **Fix:** when gating the documents step, treat the documented form.js
+   markers as blocking — e.g. if the submit carries `data-preflight-blocked`
+   or any `.field-error[data-preflight-error="true"]` is non-empty, keep the
+   applicant on that step (form.js stays untouched; the stepper only reads).
+
+4. **Medium — `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js:302-327` (`markInvalid` / `clearSatisfiedStepperErrors`) — stepper clobbers server-rendered error messages, then erases them.**
+   On the error re-render, `markInvalid` reuses the field's existing
+   `.field-error` span — which may carry the server's specific message — and
+   overwrites it with the generic `GATING_MESSAGE`, tagging it
+   `data-stepper-error`. When the field becomes merely non-empty,
+   `clearSatisfiedStepperErrors` empties the span and removes `has-error`:
+   a still server-invalid field (e.g. malformed email) renders as valid, its
+   specific guidance destroyed. The code comment above
+   `clearSatisfiedStepperErrors` ("Server-rendered messages (no
+   data-stepper-error) are never touched") is false — `markInvalid` tags
+   whatever span it finds.
+   **Fix:** in `markInvalid`, skip spans that already carry server text (only
+   fill empty or stepper-created spans), or snapshot the original
+   text/display and restore instead of blanking.
+
+5. **Medium — `server/priv/static/apply_analytics.js` interplay — `application_form_section_completed` loses truth on hidden sections.**
+   With sections 2–8 `hidden`, analytics' `hasVisibleRequired` returns false
+   for every hidden section, so its debounced `recheck` degrades to
+   "completed = interacted" for anything not currently shown. Two concrete
+   distortions vs pre-stepper: (a) reload with browser-restored values —
+   Continue gating passes on restored values with zero `input` events, so
+   those sections **never** fire `section_completed` (pre-stepper, the first
+   keystroke anywhere truthfully completed every filled section); (b)
+   Back-retreat — emptying a required field after passing, then ungated Back,
+   leaves the section hidden with `interacted=true`, firing a phantom
+   `section_completed` on the next keystroke. The funnel is a load-bearing
+   contract (spec: "funnel keys off them"); section-level completion rates
+   will shift and mislead.
+   **Fix:** without editing `apply_analytics.js`, dispatch a bubbling `input`
+   event from the section element on every gated Continue (marks it
+   `interacted` while gating guarantees completeness — completion-on-
+   interaction is then semantically correct), and document the residual
+   Back-retreat edge.
+
+6. **Medium — `scripts/js-tests/form_stepper.test.js` — spec-mandated test surface missing; the gap already let finding 2 ship.**
+   The spec's task list requires unit tests for "every I/O-matrix row + no-op
+   guards + event payload". Delivered: none for the no-op guards
+   (`data-apply-page` absent / no `application-form` → no chrome), none for
+   the `rt:form-step-changed` payload (`{step_index, section_id, total}` —
+   only the event-name constant is pinned), and none for the anchor-routing
+   click path.
+   **Fix:** add tests for the event detail shape, initBrowser no-op cases,
+   and an anchor-click routing test with real `#field-<key>` hrefs.
+
+7. **Low — `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js:143` (`resolveFieldElement`) + `error_summary.gleam` — the `gdpr_consent` summary row is unresolvable even after fixing finding 2.**
+   `anchor_for("gdpr_consent")` = `field-gdpr_consent`, but no such id or
+   `field-<key>` testid exists: the checkbox is `id="gdpr-consent"`, the
+   block `data-testid="gdpr-consent-block"` (`review_consent.gleam`). The
+   anchor was already dead on the long form (pre-existing); the stepper's
+   new router was the chance to fix it and doesn't.
+   **Fix:** special-case `gdpr_consent` → `doc.getElementById("gdpr-consent")`
+   in `resolveFieldElement`.
+
+8. **Low (pre-existing, surfaced by this feature) — `server/src/application/form_sections/documents.gleam:340` — server-rendered upload-slot errors are invisible.**
+   `view_upload_area`'s `.field-error` span never gets the inline
+   `style="display:flex"` that `form_fields.view_error_span` adds, and
+   `.field-error` is `display:none` by default (`form.css:339`) with no
+   `.has-error`-triggered reveal (upload containers never get `has-error`).
+   A server-side upload rejection therefore renders text nobody can see.
+   Pre-existing — but the stepper's error-page start-step now deliberately
+   routes applicants to the documents step to fix a message that isn't
+   visible.
+   **Fix:** add `attribute("style", "display:flex")` when `error != ""`,
+   mirroring `view_error_span`.
+
+9. **Low — `server/test/application/form_view_test.gleam:444` — the no-JS pin checks a 200-char substring, not the fieldset tag it claims to inspect.**
+   `string.slice(0, 200)` past each `<fieldset` split point will
+   false-positive the moment a legitimate inner `hidden` (e.g. documents'
+   `hidden=""` co-applicant wrapper) or any attribute value containing the
+   substring "hidden" lands within 200 chars of a fieldset start. Green
+   today only by layout accident; fails loudly for the wrong reason later.
+   **Fix:** slice to the first `">"` after `<fieldset` (or regex the tag
+   itself) before asserting `hidden` absent.
+
+10. **Low — `server/src/application/form_sections/situation.gleam:158` — new applicant-facing string inlined, against the spec's copy boundary.**
+    The spec's frozen boundary says applicant-facing strings live in
+    `server/src/copy.gleam` (whose module doc states "views never inline
+    them"); the F5 helpers went there, but the new `<summary>` text "Add
+    your current address (optional)" is inlined. The JS-side stepper strings
+    (gating line, review hint, Back/Continue) can't move — static JS — but
+    this SSR string can.
+    **Fix:** move to `copy.gleam` (e.g. `pub fn address_cluster_summary()`).
+
+11. **Low — `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js:249-258` (`updateProgress`) — on the error re-render, earlier steps render as teal "done" even when they contain server errors.**
+    Starting at the first-error step colors every previous segment
+    `stepper-segment-done` regardless of error state, contradicting the
+    banner's "a few things need your attention" for applicants whose errors
+    span multiple sections.
+    **Fix:** on `data-apply-page="form-errors"`, render unvisited segments
+    neutral (or only mark segments done once actually visited in this page
+    life).
