+# Edge Case Hunter — review-form-stepper-f1
+
+Scope: diff hunks in `review-form-stepper-f1/diff.txt` (F1 stepper + F4 field diet + F5 upload copy), every finding verified against the on-disk source before reporting. Handled paths (visibility-mirror parity with apply_analytics.js, dynamic `required` toggles, radio-group representative focus, co-applicant nested conditions, bfcache state preservation, no-JS SSR, consent submit-gate OR-logic, deletion check on `listing_source` / address quartet / helper literals) were walked and discarded silently.
+
+## Findings
+
+### 1. Error-summary anchor routing double-prefixes `field-` — every link outside the start section is dead
+
+- **Location:** `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js:438-443` (click handler) + `server/src/application/form_pages.gleam:393` + `server/src/application/error_summary.gleam` (`anchor_for`)
+- **Trigger:** Applicant clicks any error-summary link whose field is not in the initially-shown first-error section.
+- **What goes wrong:** The banner hrefs are already full anchors — `anchor_for(key)` returns `"field-" <> key`, so hrefs are `#field-email`. The handler does `id = href.slice(1)` → `"field-email"`, then calls `resolveFieldElement(doc, id)`, which prepends again: `getElementById("field-field-email")` → null; testid fallback `[data-testid="field-field-email"]` → null; `if (!target) return` exits **without** `preventDefault`. The browser's default jump targets `#field-email` inside a `hidden` (`display:none`) section — no scroll, no focus, no step switch. The click appears dead. This is the exact scenario the stepper runs on `form-errors` to fix. Only links into the starting section work (browser default, visible target). The JS tests never exercise the click handler — they call `resolveFieldElement` with raw keys only, which is why the mismatch slips through.
+- **Minimal fix:** Strip the prefix at the call site: `var target = resolveFieldElement(doc, id.replace(/^field-/, ""));` (or make `resolveFieldElement` try `doc.getElementById(key)` as-given before prepending). Add a test that passes a sliced `field-<key>` id, mirroring the real href shape.
+
+### 2. `gdpr_consent` error anchor can never resolve — no element matches `field-gdpr_consent`
+
+- **Location:** `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js:149-156` (`resolveFieldElement`) + `server/src/application/form_sections/review_consent.gleam:14` (consent input `id="gdpr-consent"`) + `server/src/application/application_handler.gleam:501-505`
+- **Trigger:** Server emits the `gdpr_consent` error (consent missing — prepended to the errors list, so it is frequently `data-first-error-field`, and the only error on no-JS/partial-JS posts where the checkbox gate never ran).
+- **What goes wrong:** The anchor is `#field-gdpr_consent`, but the checkbox's id is `gdpr-consent` and its testids are `gdpr-consent-checkbox` / `gdpr-consent-block` — neither the id lookup nor the `[data-testid="field-<key>"]` fallback can ever match, even after finding 1 is fixed. The summary link dead-ends on the browser default (no such id). The start-step logic is saved by the `.has-error` fallback (`.consent-block.has-error` lands in section 8), so the stepper still starts on the right step — but the explicit "summary links switch step + focus the field" contract fails for one of the most common single-error re-renders. Pre-existing dead anchor, but it sits squarely inside the routing surface this diff adds.
+- **Minimal fix:** Map the consent key in `resolveFieldElement`: `if (key === "gdpr_consent") return doc.getElementById("gdpr-consent");` (or add `data-testid="field-gdpr_consent"` to the consent block).
+
+### 3. Server-side upload-slot errors render `display:none` — the routed-to message is invisible
+
+- **Location:** `server/src/application/form_sections/documents.gleam:338-349` (`view_upload_area` error span) vs `server/src/application/form_fields.gleam:300` (`view_error_span` adds `style="display:flex"`) + `server/priv/static/form.css:339` (`.field-error { display: none; }`)
+- **Trigger:** Error re-render carrying a server upload error — `landlord_ref_primary` / `character_ref_primary` / `employer_ref_*` required-miss, or per-file/aggregate rejections from `upload_errors_from_prepare`.
+- **What goes wrong:** The slot's `.field-error` span gets the message text but never the inline `display:flex` that every other field renderer applies — so the inline error the applicant is being routed to is invisible. The stepper's `firstErrorIndex` third fallback exists precisely for these slots ("upload slots never get .has-error — their container class is static SSR"), so the diff routes the applicant to the documents step and focuses a file input with no visible statement of what's wrong. Pre-existing SSR gap, but the diff's error-routing feature is the first thing whose success depends on it, and the fix is one mirrored attribute.
+- **Minimal fix:** In `view_upload_area`, mirror `view_error_span`: add `attribute("style", "display:flex")` to the span's attribute list when `error != ""`.
+
+### 4. Preflight-blocked submit is an invisible dead-end on the final step
+
+- **Location:** `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js:363-385` (`onContinue` — no preflight check) + `server/priv/static/form.js:469,491,518-519` (preflight sets `data-preflight-blocked`, banner lives inside the documents section)
+- **Trigger:** Applicant stages oversized files (per-file >5MB or aggregate >22MB) on the documents step; preflight disables submit via `data-preflight-blocked` and shows the aggregate banner inside section 7. Gating passes (file inputs are "satisfied" — `files.length > 0`), Continue advances to step 8.
+- **What goes wrong:** On step 8 the submit button is disabled by the OR-gate (`data-consent-blocked || data-preflight-blocked`), but the explanation — the aggregate banner, and any inline per-file message — is hidden inside section 7. Ticking/unticking consent never re-enables the button and nothing on the visible step says why. Pre-stepper the banner was always somewhere on the same scrollable page; the stepper's section-hiding creates the dead-end. Recoverable only if the applicant guesses to click Back.
+- **Minimal fix:** In `onContinue`, when the current section contains file inputs and submit carries `data-preflight-blocked`, stay on the step (scroll the preflight banner into view) instead of advancing: `var sub = doc.querySelector('[data-testid="submit-application"]'); if (sections[i].el.querySelector('input[type="file"]') && sub && sub.hasAttribute("data-preflight-blocked")) { return; }`.
+
+### 5. No guard that form.js ran — a failed form.js fetch turns gating into a hard block
+
+- **Location:** `server/priv/static/form_stepper.js:191-196` (`initBrowser` — no dependency check) + SSR-visible conditional wrappers, e.g. `server/src/application/form_sections/guarantor.gleam:101-107` (`guarantor-fields`, `required: True` fields, no SSR `hidden`) and `server/src/application/form_sections/references.gleam` (character-ref trio, `required: True`, no SSR `hidden`)
+- **Trigger:** `form_stepper.js` loads but `form.js` doesn't (independent script fetches on flaky mobile connections — 80% of form traffic) or dies on a runtime error before its condition engine init.
+- **What goes wrong:** SSR renders the conditional wrappers visible (only the condition engine hides them). The stepper's gating rule is "all visible required controls filled", so step 4 demands landlord trio **and** character trio simultaneously, and step 5 demands the full guarantor block (`guarantor_name`, relationship, phone, email, income, employer — all `required: True`) from applicants with no guarantor. The no-JS fallback can't rescue this — JS is on, the stepper owns navigation, and the Continue gate never passes. The stepper converts a partial JS degradation (long form still submittable without form.js: `novalidate`, server authoritative) into a total failure on exactly the cohort the feature targets.
+- **Minimal fix:** Bail to the long form when the condition engine never ran, e.g. at the top of `initBrowser`: `if (typeof root.__rtRecomputeSubmitDisabled !== "function") return;` — no chrome, no gating, form behaves as no-stepper.
+
+## Deletion check (Step 4)
+
+Walked the removed/replaced code: the address quartet is re-established field-for-field inside `view_address_cluster` (same names, types, required-ness, `autocomplete` via `autocomplete_for`); `listing_source` server acceptance is intact (`is_valid_listing_source` keeps `""`, the whitelist const, parity test, `error_summary` label, DB column — verified at `application_handler.gleam:1089`); F5 helper literals are re-established via `copy.gleam` in all seven slots. No orphaned references and no retired contract beyond the spec-mandated UI removal of the select. No deletion findings.
+
+**Total findings: 5**
